WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.040
<b>The Man with a Secret Power</b>

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.640
<i>This is the comics section.</i>

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.850
<i>A battleground, devoid of morality.</i>

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.510
<i>By some tragic mistake,</i>

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.580
<i>a youngster from a different 
department transferred over here.</i>

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.790
I look forward to working with all of you.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.160
Kendo-san

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.160
I'm Kendo.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.540
I was originally in Distribution, 
so I don't know much about retail.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.530
I hope you teach me well.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.980
Welcome!

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.000
<i>Such a kind voice.</i>

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.680
Good work today.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.400
<i>A graceful demeanor, always 
accompanied by a smile.</i>

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:44.840
<i>Crap, he's more refined than all 
the girls in the comics section.</i>

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.800
<i>In Kendo-san's original
 department, Distribution,</i>

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:53.420
<b>* Artist rendition</b>

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:53.420
<b>Distribution</b>

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:52.800
<i>the overwhelming majority of
 the work was heavy labor.</i>

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.400
<i>As a result, despite his lean figure,</i>

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.730
<i>Kendo-san has no trouble lifting 
super-heavy cardboard boxes.</i>

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:02.600
<b>Up we go!</b>

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.880
<i>And every time he does, we're left in awe.</i>

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.730
You're amazing!

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.570
It's nothing.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.300
I'm glad I'm apparently being useful.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.550
He's so awesome.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.380
The men are smitten!

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.780
<i>In said Distribution division,</i>

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.400
<i>there is a living legend of a man...</i>

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.560
<i>His name is Assistant Manager Majutsushi.</i>

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.050
Distribution 
Assistant Manager Majutsushi

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.100
Crap, crap, we're sold out.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.020
Normally, the people in charge 
at the storefront make orders.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.060
Oh, hello, hi, uhh... err...

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.360
Do you have that thing that's 
called, like, "Pop Poop Peptic"?

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.030
<b>** Award Winner</b>

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.030
<b>A Star Has Fallen</b>

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.750
<i>When the world is struck by shortage,</i>

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.400
<i>Assistant Manager Majutsushi casts 
his special summoning spell.</i>

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.270
Hello? It's me.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.650
Books, please.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.280
<i>And with that incantation,</i>

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.570
<i>incredible amounts of books arrive 
at the store with incredible speed.</i>

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:54.780
Good mor—

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.580
<b>Agh!</b>

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.580
Oh, Honda, morning.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.110
What the heck happened here?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.720
Haven't you seen the news?

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.400
You know, about the revered 
author of <i>Ki**ro</i>...

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.880
Oh, right, he passed away, didn't he?

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.660
Wait, does that mean this is all...

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.900
Yeah, these are all the author's books.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.990
I can't believe you got so much so quickly.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.870
Assistant Manager Majutsushi 
never fails to amaze me.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.750
He must be keeping an eye on
 all kinds of information.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.300
<i>His ability to make orders that 
a person from the shop couldn't</i>

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.290
<i>is nothing short of magic.</i>

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.630
<i>When the world is shaken by 
news, whether good or bad,</i>

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.290
<i>Assistant Manager Majutsushi 
is quietly hard at work.</i>

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.190
There it is.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.290
That's the one.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.370
Have you read this manga, mister bookseller?

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.570
I'm embarrassed to admit I haven't.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.570
It's so good.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.920
I saw the news on TV, and 
I got kind of depressed.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.940
He's about my age.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.920
I like the famous ones he wrote for children,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.380
but I never thought I'd find this one.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.780
<i>I wonder if the busy Assistant 
Manager Majutsushi is aware...</i>

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:14.050
<i>That the customers who pick up the books
 at the store smile so blissfully.</i>

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.810
The products we ordered were damaged!

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:18.710
Where's <i>Aku**-kun</i>?!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.470
<i>Aku**-kun</i>!

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.290
At the storefront?

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.860
Nope, but the system says it's in stock!

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.230
Which means...

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.570
Somewhere in here

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.570
Please tell me you're kidding!

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.850
Hello.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.080
Patrol time.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.920
I can't find it!

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.480
Where did you put it?!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.480
Keep them sorted by title, dammit!

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.190
It seems like it's always so
 much fun in the Comics section.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.420
I'm sorry, would you mind 
helping us open the boxes?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.490
Sure.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.000
<b>Our Fair-Day War</b>

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.330
<b>Anime adaptation announced!! 
Guess who the voice actor is!</b>

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.330
An anime?!

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.870
<b>TV Drama and Movie Adaptation Announced</b>

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.870
<b>Original manga</b>

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.650
A movie?!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.090
A stageplay?!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.330
<b>Stageplay announced!</b>

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.900
<b>Smash!</b>

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.900
<b>* No actual hitting involved</b>

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.690
So many fair proposals.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.180
Let's get the big ones out of the way first.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.700
Honda-san, keep record, please.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.880
Please don't leave me behind.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.390
It's <i>your</i> job to keep up!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:11.880
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:18.750
<b>Literary Greats Revival Fair</b>

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:18.750
<b>Banners</b>

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:18.750
<b>Horror Stories and Mysteries 
from All Times and Places</b>

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:18.750
<b>Stacks</b>

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.370
<i>Fairs are fun events where shops, booksellers</i>

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.340
<i>and publishers show off their creativity.</i>

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.680
Still, though, is there 
any point to doing fairs?

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.760
They should sell fine if the books
 and location are in order.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:32.310
Well, don't we want to set ourselves 
apart from other bookstores?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.850
What do you mean?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.410
Come on up!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:41.810
Like a fresh food shop

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.470
Get your fresh <i>Oso*****-san</i> here!

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.840
The manga that the movie's based on?

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.110
You've got good taste, sir!

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:54.050
Like a cosmetics shop

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.800
Are you looking for anything 
in particular, ma'am?

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.040
Please sample this new book if you'd ilke.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.400
I recommend this piece,

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.050
which exploded online and 
by word-of-mouth overnight.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.780
Like, a pushier style.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.380
That's scary.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:00.770
No one expects a bookseller to talk 
to them when they're shopping.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.220
I heard the chefs come to the 
table at restaurants overseas.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.000
Oh, I've seen that before.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.650
So what if we did something like...

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.400
Enjoying your book, sir?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.560
We'd cause a huge controversy!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.910
I hate how you say it, too!

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.540
Even if there's a book you really recommend,

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.560
it's not strategic for a bookseller 
to talk to a customer.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.120
As if that weren't obvious.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.890
So this one's getting an anime, 
and this one's getting a drama.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.700
Nothing but mixed media, huh?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.110
That's not all.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.120
Like this one, here.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.700
Um...

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.200
Sorry, they're all movie adaptations!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.130
They're all adaptations!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.380
No problem.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.610
We just have to add extras.

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.540
It won't be a big deal.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.640
Easy peasy.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.170
That's true, too.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:49.570
Movie Adaptation Fair

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:49.570
<b>Anime Adaptation</b>

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:49.570
<i>We were strangely calm at the time.</i>

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:53.480
** Bookstore

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:53.480
<b>A few days later...</b>

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.840
<i>That is, until the moment the fair was announced.</i>

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:57.110
I'm sorry, I'm not at liberty to reveal 
our stock count outside of the company.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.920
Huh? "Just tell you secretly"? 
I can't, I'm sorry.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:04.490
However, we have plenty of copies, so we ask 
that you refrain from lining up before we open.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.650
You want <i>just</i> the bonuses?

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:06.620
I see, I understand.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.790
No can do!

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.790
They're revealing their greed.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:13.110
Well, when a photo of the cast 
is the included bonus...

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.220
Understood, we will make an effort 
not to get our fingerprints on it.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.520
They don't want us to even touch it?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.590
All right, we look forward to seeing you.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:25.100
I'm afraid of the phone! I wanna go home!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.510
Stay!

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.420
You're doing great!

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:31.980
Fair Leader 
Lantern-senpai

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.530
The bonus media will be 
sealed along with the covers

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.980
<b>Movie Announced</b>

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.980
so it's clear that the book 
comes with a bonus.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:40.160
<b>Front</b>

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.010
They're reversibles, with illustrations are 
on the front and cast photos on the back.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:40.160
<b>Back</b>

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.450
Please put them in so that the 
illustration side is visible.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.160
We don't want the photos visible?

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:44.810
We want to avoid them drawing too much 
attention and get taken without a sale.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:45.420
I see.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.260
Gotcha.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.110
<i>What the hell?!</i>

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.840
<i>This is the </i>Yama**-kun<i> bookmark!</i>

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.230
<i>This isn't what I was promised!</i>

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.930
P-Please look on the back!

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.340
<i>Oh, yay! It's a reversible! Thank goodness.</i>

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.930
Excuse me!

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.290
I saw this store on the list of distributors.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.820
Don't you have the <i>Yama**-kun</i> bookmarks?!

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.350
Don't tell me you're out of them already!

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.130
Oh, my, there's a picture 
on the backside, too.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.260
Oh dear, I rushed to conclusions.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.350
May I have a new bookmark?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.260
Honda, have you aged?

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:24.270
<i>We learned that movie adaptations starring 
idols wreak havoc on people's minds.</i>

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.690
<b>The fair list is done</b>

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:29.390
Okitsune-senpai, are we doing an 
anthropomorphic cells manga fair?

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.760
In charge of Kou-D-sha

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:30.000
Yeah.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.120
Awesome!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:31.760
I can't wait!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.210
I'm going to buy the new book!

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.510
<b>Yay!</b>

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.510
<b>Boss</b>

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.510
<b>Dark orders from above 
You must do a <i>Cells</i>-based fair</b>

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.070
I mean, I'm just doing it 
'cause I was asked to.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.800
Thank you for your business.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:45.350
In charge of Kadokawa men's comics

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:45.350
In charge of subculture and 4-koma

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.510
We're doing a <i>Jingai</i> fair?

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.000
Sounds fun!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.310
We need to order the ones that are out of stock.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:46.060
Oh, right.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.690
Right, the anime adaptation sets are coming.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:52.260
<b>Set 

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:51.220
Wait, Shu-E-sha's sets are already here!

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.260
It's too much!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.200
In charge of Shu-E-sha

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.320
The specials are bookmarks.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:54.860
Again?

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.900
Shu-E-sha's really into bookmarks, huh?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:01.290
Wow, the dyed paper for the fair is so pretty!

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:04.970
In charge of women's comics

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:04.970
In charge of game guides

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.270
I know, right?

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.970
I bet a lot of people will want photos.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:14.610
<b>Pandemonium</b>

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:14.610
<b>Serious BL</b>

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:14.610
In charge of BL

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:10.610
Wanna talk about the time we got a bunch of draft 
copies, and most of them were for sex scenes?

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:10.610
How...

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.240
How are we supposed to spin that?!

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.340
It's funny, but please don't!

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.320
Honda-san.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:21.750
In charge of light novels 
Yosetsu Mask-san

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:18.850
Yosetsu Mask-san.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.750
Are you not getting American 
comic posters or anything yet?

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:23.640
They aren't coming in.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.540
Apparently it's been 
complicated by rights issues.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.430
Oh...

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:33.530
<b>Heh, heh...</b>

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.080
I was hoping to enjoy them after work.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.040
<i>There's a fan among us!</i>

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.050
** Bookstore

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.300
** Bookstore

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.540
Now, then...

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.930
Let's get started.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:54.790
<i>Both staff and customers ask whether 
there's a point to doing fairs.</i>

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.990
<i>But this is the best part of a bookstore.</i>

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:06.830
<b>Staff Picks</b>

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:03.910
<i>My fairs aren't very creative, 
with just hand-made pop-ups.</i>

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.350
<i>But it's pretty fun preparing them.</i>

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.120
Good work today.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.640
Kendo-san.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.270
That's a lot of hand-drawn pop-ups.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:19.440
They're work supplies, so 
I can use them liberally.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.310
Wow, I wouldn't have thought 
the rationale was stinginess.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:28.640
<b>Staff Picks</b>

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:27.370
<i>It's all good if people get the 
sense that we're having fun.</i>
